</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.4 Analysis of Intervention Words Catagories ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Active Confusion Expression in Large Language Models: Leveraging World Models toward Better Social Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, our selected intervention words (Ours) achieve optimal performance in both accuracy and token efficiency across all datasets compared to other common intervention words (+PV and +BE). This indicates that compared to choosing simple pause-validation or branch-extension words for interruption, our method demonstrates good methodological stability and applicability, which also validates the conclusions in section <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS1" title="3.2.1 Cognitive Intervention ‣ 3.2 Adaptive World Model-Enhanced Reasoning with Cognitive Intervention ‣ 3 Method ‣ Active Confusion Expression in Large Language Models: Leveraging World Models toward Better Social Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Analysis of Other Methods</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the effectiveness of our method in improving reasoning performance, we compare our method with several approaches for enhancing model reasoning capabilities, including Chain-of-Thought (CoT), Tree of Thoughts (ToT)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2023a</a>)</cite>, Reasoning and Acting (ReAct) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2023b</a>)</cite>, and Reflexion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shinn et al., 2023</a>)</cite> for comparative evaluation.</p>
</div>
